{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Deploy the supplied PostgreSQL schema and records as database branch_stock on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied SQL created both tables and inserted all four rows. Final and post-restart queries show the expected stock and supplier-cost records in branch_stock with PostgreSQL active.","evidence_ids":["cmd-26476ca1a98c4d6d","cmd-351e0f7e681a48d4","cmd-5d19d4cb85654ff4","cmd-598ab3c5829c45a2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow stock_app from node2 to read stock and update only stock quantities, without schema changes or access to supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote behavioral tests demonstrated stock reads and a transactional quantity update, while supplier_costs reads, table creation, and SKU updates were denied. Final privilege inspection and post-restart remote access confirmed the intended restrictions persisted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-80e5111f1eca44ec","cmd-ffdf027872de47be","cmd-95416d407a084dc0","cmd-5d19d4cb85654ff4","cmd-63d255954aba472d","cmd-598ab3c5829c45a2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Give auditor read-only access to stock and supplier_costs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The auditor successfully read a join of both tables, an attempted stock update was denied, and final catalog inspection showed SELECT on both tables without stock UPDATE. Access remained functional after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a923d35f924d4f65","cmd-83546f1f27d64556","cmd-5d19d4cb85654ff4","cmd-afce3e7fc67d41ec","cmd-598ab3c5829c45a2"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Establish separate credentials for stock_app and auditor on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Separate role-specific password files were created on node2 with root-only mode 600, both roles authenticated independently, and PostgreSQL reported SCRAM credentials and restricted node2-only HBA entries. The files and successful authentications survived node2's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-351e0f7e681a48d4","cmd-9ddd0acf6bc442d3","cmd-7fafebe5dbf448ee","cmd-55c1622fe7a64669","cmd-afce3e7fc67d41ec","cmd-598ab3c5829c45a2"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the supplied records in /srv/legacy2/database-reader-writer-roles.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The stock.sql SHA-256 remained identical to the preparation baseline on both nodes, including after their restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-26476ca1a98c4d6d","cmd-5d19d4cb85654ff4","cmd-afce3e7fc67d41ec"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8 before and after execution and restart. PostgreSQL 13 packages were installed from the RHEL 9 AppStream repositories, and package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a440d14ad42f4a67","cmd-c32effd6ecc040ca","cmd-e334dfe35e0a498f","cmd-cc9cdaf4ede7404d","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All observed mutations had clear implementation, verification, restart-protocol, or cleanup roles; no causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. Temporary SSH authorization and server-side plaintext credential files were removed. One low-impact import log remained at /tmp/branch_stock_import.log after its evidentiary use. PostgreSQL's new listener was task-required and constrained by a node2-only firewall rule and role-specific HBA entries; no failed services or package-health damage appeared. The trace cannot establish whether deleting the whole node1 root known_hosts file affected pre-existing entries, so this is an uncertainty rather than a confirmed hygiene defect.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70a3911f375d484a","cmd-7fafebe5dbf448ee","cmd-9ae4cfdb4b7b4dc8","cmd-351e0f7e681a48d4","cmd-6bb69e8809c242c4","cmd-55c1622fe7a64669","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral and final-state evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was completed coherently on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity, an acknowledged scheduled restart, a different post-restart identity, and recovered service, credentials, data, privileges, and remote access. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["The final distinct-password comparison output was redacted, although independently generated role-specific files, separate SCRAM roles, and successful authentication by both roles strongly support credential separation.","No direct evidence establishes whether /root/.ssh/known_hosts on node1 contained pre-existing entries before it was removed during cleanup.","The auditor denial test exercised UPDATE on stock rather than supplier_costs; supplier_costs read-only status is supported by the recorded grants, PUBLIC revocation, non-superuser role state, and final privilege observations rather than a direct denied supplier_costs update attempt."]}
